The derived file was changed for sandbox-runtime: unsupported architecture
mappings and capability-gated rules were removed, and the explicit Chromium
user-namespace sandbox rule was limited to chroot, clone, setns, and unshare.
Unlike the pinned original, which gates chroot on CAP_SYS_CHROOT, this
Browser-specific derived rule permits the chroot syscall without that
seccomp capability condition. The executable Chromium sandbox uses it for
sys_chroot("/proc/self/fdinfo/") during zygote setup. This is a deliberate
seccomp difference, not proof that the initial non-root container process
can chroot or that another workload may reuse the policy. The opt-in real
Docker A/B diagnostic in chroot_ab_integration_test.go tests that boundary;
the full Phase 6 topology and application gate are separate.
